{"kind":"panel","id":"12758aaa-862c-4d0e-bc60-3fff16897536","type":"59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c","name":"Panel","nick":"Tank modes","desc":"A panel for custom notes and text values","box":[300,60,900,200],"src":[],"text":"Tank modes - a concrete tank's first hundred natural modes, side by side.\n\nA cylinder 4 m across and 5 m tall, its concrete wall 200 mm thick, built in round its base and open at the top, as ASD Shells. The Natural Vibration Analysis finds its first Modes modes, its own weight the mass that swings.\n\nModel View takes every mode at once: a Series of steps, 0 for the first, into its Step. It draws only the last, so its preview is off; its Geometry output, a coloured mesh a mode, is moved onto a grid, Columns to a row, and drawn by the Mesh parameter Every mode, with each mode's number and frequency under it. A round tank's modes come in pairs, the same shape turned round by half a wave: they have the same frequency.","colour":[255,255,250,90]}
